                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "03fcd534-5105-3913-b56d-45d3d72cab4b",
                        "entry_id": "f3d51383-f8a0-389b-8203-f381743f8115",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To place in contraposition."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e34c713e-f9e7-410c-8663-06ec19018715",
                                "sense_id": "03fcd534-5105-3913-b56d-45d3d72cab4b",
                                "text": "We certainly do not want to take our simple categorical statements and contrapose them into cumbersome natural language."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c804206-ea4e-47da-b8d7-65eee68876a9",
                                "sense_id": "03fcd534-5105-3913-b56d-45d3d72cab4b",
                                "text": "To contrapose an argument one swaps the conclusion with any one of the premisses and negates each of the swapped statements."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "218dea5e-a08b-4029-be1b-fc7f3daf7549",
                                "sense_id": "03fcd534-5105-3913-b56d-45d3d72cab4b",
                                "text": "But subjunctive conditionals do not contrapose, and we are misled into accepting a sensitivity condition by confusing it with a safety condition."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4accc065-e763-31ea-9d15-afd592dbd725",
                        "entry_id": "f3d51383-f8a0-389b-8203-f381743f8115",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To contrast with, or form an opposite to, something."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2951f32-455a-4e15-9de6-2fb05ed1e64a",
                                "sense_id": "4accc065-e763-31ea-9d15-afd592dbd725",
                                "text": "At such moments, King was contraposed against the more frightening threat, his symbolism making the radicalism of the other party all the more apparent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8ee128bb-8e37-486c-ae90-e007dd993bbb",
                                "sense_id": "4accc065-e763-31ea-9d15-afd592dbd725",
                                "text": "In fact, whereas the term existence is contraposed to non-existence, the term factual or empirical is contraposed to essential;"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
